                <pb facs="0307" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg297"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 18.</seg></opener>
                <head>Messrs. Sinclair, Hamilton &amp; Co. to Earl
                        Russell.—(Received February 8.)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>11 <hi rendition="#small-caps">St. Helen’s
                            Place,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-08"><hi rendition="#italic">London,
                                February</hi> 8, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> Referring to our letter of 29th
                    January, as to the capture of the bark Saxon by the United States steamer
                    Vanderbilt, we have now the honor to inform your lordship that the Saxon, at the
                    time of capture, was at anchor within a mile and a half of Penguin island,
                    British territory.</p>
                <p>We have &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>SINCLAIR, HAMILTON &amp; CO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
